ELECTRICITY_USAGE_MYSQL Project Description
The ELECTRICITY_USAGE_MYSQL project is a database-driven system designed to efficiently store, manage, and analyze electricity consumption data using MySQL.
The primary objective of this project is to help monitor electricity usage, track consumption patterns, and generate meaningful reports that can assist users and administrators in making informed energy management decisions.
This system maintains detailed records of electricity usage collected from individual meters or users on a daily or monthly basis.
It stores essential information such as user details, meter readings, billing periods, and tariff rates.
By organizing this data in a structured relational database, the project ensures data accuracy, consistency, and easy retrieval.
The project allows administrators to perform operations such as inserting new meter readings, updating user information, and managing tariff details.
Users can view their electricity consumption history, identify peak usage periods, and estimate electricity costs based on recorded data.
SQL queries are used to calculate total consumption, generate monthly and yearly reports, and analyze usage trends.
Overall, the ELECTRICITY_USAGE_MYSQL project demonstrates the practical application of MySQL in real-world energy management systems.
It highlights core database concepts such as table relationships, primary and foreign keys, normalization, and query optimization while addressing the growing need for efficient electricity usage monitoring.
